1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,063
A CFO gets a video call from the CEO,
travelling in Europe.

2
00:00:04,435 --> 00:00:05,132
Looks right.

3
00:00:05,445 --> 00:00:06,339
Sounds right.

4
00:00:06,769 --> 00:00:08,824
Wants a quarter of a million dollars.

5
00:00:09,323 --> 00:00:10,820
The acquisition is real.

6
00:00:11,192 --> 00:00:12,875
Weeks of negotiations.

7
00:00:13,468 --> 00:00:16,312
The caller says legal has cleared the
deposit:

8
00:00:16,625 --> 00:00:18,576
two hundred and fifty thousand dollars,

9
00:00:18,599 --> 00:00:21,548
within thirty minutes, or the seller can
walk.

10
00:00:22,047 --> 00:00:23,255
They know the target.

11
00:00:23,754 --> 00:00:26,180
Yesterday's confidential board discussion.

12
00:00:26,552 --> 00:00:28,491
A director's private concern.

13
00:00:28,990 --> 00:00:31,463
Even the CFO's upcoming vacation.

14
00:00:31,892 --> 00:00:33,541
The wire instructions arrive

15
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:36,014
from the CEO's real corporate email.

16
00:00:36,443 --> 00:00:38,347
The receiving bank account is new.

17
00:00:38,777 --> 00:00:41,261
Company policy requires two executives

18
00:00:41,319 --> 00:00:43,746
for anything over one hundred thousand
dollars.

19
00:00:44,338 --> 00:00:47,995
The second authorized executive is on a
flight, unreachable.

20
00:00:48,495 --> 00:00:51,583
A call to the CEO's known mobile gets no
answer.

21
00:00:52,012 --> 00:00:53,150
All that detail.

22
00:00:53,464 --> 00:00:55,844
Still a decision someone has to own.

23
00:00:56,436 --> 00:00:58,282
What should the CFO do?
